      "target": "../sections/sec-007-311-study-characteristics.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Study characteristics \nStudies included were those that evaluated the performance of the most recent generation of \ncommercial, RD1 antigen based IGRAs (QuantiFERON-TB Gold In-Tube (QFT-GIT) [Celestis, Victoria, \nAustralia] and T-SPOT [Oxford Immunotec, Oxford, United Kingdom]) among adult (>15 years) active \npulmonary TB suspects or cases in low- and middle-income countries. \n \nStudies excluded were those that evaluated non-commercial IGRAs, PPD-based IGRAs, \nQuantiFERON-TB Gold (2G), IGRAs performed in specimens other than blood; those reporting \nlongitudinal data focused on the effect of an",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the studies included on IGRAs for diagnosing active pulmonary TB in adults in low- and middle-income countries, limited to the two current commercial assays. It explains how sensitivity and specificity were estimated, the latter only among suspects found not to have active TB.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
