      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Strengths and limitations of the evidence base",
      "pageStart": 16,
      "pageEnd": 17,
      "target": "../sections/sec-009-313-strengths-and-limitations-of-the-evidence-ba.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Strengths and limitations of the evidence base \nHeterogeneity was substantial for the primary outcomes of sensitivity and specificity.  Empirical \nrandom effects weighting, excluding studies contributing fewer than 10 eligible individuals, and \nseparately synthesizing data for currently manufactured IGRAs were performed in order to minimize \nheterogeneity.  \n \nNo standard criteria exist for defining high TB incidence countries and the World Bank income \nclassification is an imperfect surrogate for national TB incidence; nevertheless, results were \nfundamentally unchanged when restricted to cou",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the strengths and limitations of the evidence on IGRAs for active TB, including substantial heterogeneity and the steps taken to reduce it. It also notes the lack of standard definitions of high-incidence settings and of data on patient outcomes or preferences.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
