    {
      "id": "library/10665-44759/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Grade evidence profiles and final policy recommendations",
      "pageStart": 17,
      "pageEnd": 18,
      "target": "../sections/sec-010-314-grade-evidence-profiles-and-final-policy-rec.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Grade evidence profiles and final policy recommendations \nThe GRADE evidence profiles are provided in Tables 1 and 2. Based on these assessments, the Expert \nGroup concluded that the quality of evidence for use of IGRAs and the TST in diagnosis of active TB \nwas low and recommended that these tests should not be used in low- and middle-income countries \nas a replacement for conventional microbiological diagnosis of pulmonary and extra-pulmonary TB \n(strong recommendation).  \n \nThe Expert Group also noted that current evidence did not support the use of IGRAs or the TST as \npart of the diagnost",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents the Expert Group's conclusion that evidence for IGRAs and the skin test in diagnosing active TB was of low quality. It gives the strong recommendation against using them instead of microbiological diagnosis in low- and middle-income countries, given the harm of false positives.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
