      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Study characteristics \nThe initial search yielded 234 citations. After full-text review of 68 papers evaluating IGRAs in \nchildren, 32 were determined to meet eligibility criteria, covering 33 unique evaluations of one or \nmore IGRAs (hereafter referred to as studies) in 18 countries. Of the 33 studies, three were from \nlow-income countries, and 11 were from middle-income countries.  The incidence of smear-positive \nTB was <25/100,000 in 18 of these countries and >=25/100,000 in the remaining countries. Studies \nperformed in high-income countries included between 11% and 100% immigrant childre",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the studies on IGRAs in children found through the literature search, covering evaluations in 18 countries. Only a minority came from low- and middle-income countries, and definitions of TB suspects and controls varied.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
