      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Strengths and limitations of the evidence base",
      "pageStart": 19,
      "pageEnd": 20,
      "target": "../sections/sec-014-323-strengths-and-limitations-of-the-evidence-ba.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Strengths and limitations of the evidence base \nStudies included assessed very different populations in diverse settings, with the biggest challenge \nand limitation related to major differences in methodological approaches across studies and non-\nstandardised definitions of reference standards, TB exposure and TB disease.   \n \nSample sizes in the different studies varied greatly and were less than ten in some of the subgroups \nanalysed, which adversely impact on generalisability of the findings.  \n \nEmpirical random effects weighting and separately synthesizing data for currently manufactured",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes limitations of the paediatric evidence, including very different populations, methods and non-standard reference definitions. Sample sizes were often small, and no data were available on patient outcomes or preferences.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
